.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
tests/
pytest.ini
.pytest_cache/

# Committed databases — must never reach an image. Untracked by git but they
# DO exist on disk in every working checkout (spendly.db, spendly-backup.db at
# the repo root today), and .gitignore does not filter a Docker build context
# — only this file does. WAL mode (phase 0) can also leave -wal/-shm sidecar
# files next to the DB while the app is running; both excluded too.
#
# `**/` prefix is deliberate, not decorative: verified by build that a bare
# `*.db` here only matches at the build-context ROOT in this Docker/BuildKit
# version, not recursively like a .gitignore pattern. A probe file placed at
# database/_probe.db leaked straight into an image layer under a bare `*.db`
# rule and was only caught once changed to `**/*.db`. `database/spendly.db`
# is exactly the kind of nested path .gitignore's own comment says used to be
# tracked, so root-only matching here is not a hypothetical risk.
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm

.env
.DS_Store
file.txt
test.md
*.stackdump
README.md
docs/
